 Everything is typed TypeScript content. `tsc` refuses a registry entry with a missing field or a status outside the six the constitution allows. `scripts/verify-cluster.mjs` enforces the rules the type system cannot: a KPI with a value but no measurement date, an `ARCHIVE` without a kill-list entry, a scored workflow without evidence, a conversation marked as validation.
 
+## Visualization
+
+`components/viz/` — ClusterMap, ContractSequence, MaturityLadder, StatusBars, Funnel, ObjectiveRing, PeriodTimeline, ScoreHeatmap, Sparkline, PulseBoard. All server components emitting inline SVG: no chart library, no client JavaScript, native `<title>` hover, `role="img"` labels and figcaption legends. Colours are CSS tokens (`--viz-*`) validated for colour-vision deficiency and contrast in both themes (categorical: Operations `#178A62`, Energy `#2a78d6`, Physical AI `#c2571f`; dark steps `#2AA078 / #4489e2 / #d96a33`); text always wears text tokens, never the series colour. The commit pulse is read from GitHub's `stats/commit_activity` at build time and revalidated twice a day; when GitHub has not computed it or is unreachable, the sparkline is absent, not flat.
+
+## Agentic discoverability
+
+An agent that lands anywhere on the host can find everything: every response carries `Link: </.well-known/api-catalog>; rel="api-catalog"` and `rel="service-desc"` to `/openapi.json`; the HTML head links `/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt`, `/ai.txt`, `/api/cluster/`, the OpenAPI document, the API catalog and both Atom feeds as `<link rel="alternate">`; `robots.txt` names and allows every documented AI crawler; JSON-LD (`WebSite`, `CollectionPage`, `Dataset`, `SoftwareSourceCode`, `BreadcrumbList`) is on every page; the read-only API allows cross-origin `GET`. `/ai.txt` states what may be quoted and what must not be claimed (no revenue or customer figures unless `/api/cluster/kpi/` shows a measured value).
+
 ## The evidence rule
 
 - A KPI is `null` until measured. The UI renders `null` as "not yet measured", never as 0.
diff --git a/app/.well-known/api-catalog/route.ts b/app/.well-known/api-catalog/route.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6515f1c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/.well-known/api-catalog/route.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+import { ENDPOINTS } from '@/lib/cluster-api';
+import { SITE_URL } from '@/lib/site';
+
+export const dynamic = 'force-static';
+
+/**
+ * /.well-known/api-catalog — RFC 9727 API catalog, as a linkset (RFC 9264).
+ *
+ * The standard way for a client to discover which APIs a host publishes:
+ * one JSON document listing every API with its OpenAPI description and
+ * documentation. Advertised from every response with a
+ * `Link: </.well-known/api-catalog>; rel="api-catalog"` header (vercel.json).
+ */
+export function GET() {
+  const linkset = {
+    linkset: [
+      {
+        anchor: `${SITE_URL}/api/cluster/`,
+        'service-desc': [{ href: `${SITE_URL}/openapi.json`, type: 'application/vnd.oai.openapi+json;version=3.1' }],
+        'service-doc': [{ href: `${SITE_URL}/cluster/map/`, type: 'text/html' }, { href: `${SITE_URL}/llms.txt`, type: 'text/plain' }],
+        'service-meta': [{ href: `${SITE_URL}/api/cluster/schema/`, type: 'application/schema+json' }, { href: `${SITE_URL}/ai.txt`, type: 'text/plain' }],
+        status: [{ href: `${SITE_URL}/api/cluster/roadmap/`, type: 'application/json' }],
+        item: ENDPOINTS.map((e) => ({ href: `${SITE_URL}${e.path}`, title: e.summary })),
+      },
+    ],
+  };
+  return new Response(JSON.stringify(linkset, null, 2), {
+    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/linkset+json; charset=utf-8', 'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800' },
+  });
+}
